But then, as the game continues and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> has the ball, about to score, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Patrick</span> <span style="color:LightCoral">suddenly trips on his shoelace and tumbles right into the boy, knocking them both to the ground and causing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> to miss his kick.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Whoops, haha, sorry about that!”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Patrick</span> giggles, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Guess my shoes got untied.”</span>  <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, you should pay more attention!”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> shouts back, angry that his shot had been screwed up. He looks <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Patrick</span> up and down and smirks, wanting to get a little payback. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Tripping me like that, that’s not very good teamwork. Want to see what I do to bad teammates?”</span>  <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Patrick</span> holds a finger up to his mouth and tilts his head, confused about what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Michael</span> is talking about. <br>

